  "interpretation": [
    "Retention fixes preserve all tested bounded execution, pressure rejection, same-pool recovery and cache/transport behavior.",
    "Including post-release and final-eviction snapshots, native R2 samples 97,687,612 managed-heap bytes at a 64 MiB admission pool and 179,062,576 at 128 MiB with four jobs. Whole-runtime cap acceptance is contradicted by these samples.",
    "Post-eviction diagnostic GC reduces managed heap to approximately 5 MB with 366,064 backing bytes. This supports pending reclamation, not a large surviving leak in this fixture; production cannot depend on forced GC.",
    "Managed-heap-constrained HTTP completes, but the V8 flag does not bound external backing or total Worker memory. Counter maxima are recorded separately and are not assumed additive.",
    "Sparse GC-dependent measurements are lower bounds on peaks, not statistical before/after improvements or proof that retention fixes caused a particular peak change.",
    "Broader allocation coverage, operator scheduling and runtime headroom remain open."
  ],
